vernance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["CareTrust REIT, Inc. is a mid-cap real estate business with a $9.8B market cap on $476M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +34% over the past three years and +20% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 8.4\u00d7.","Net dilution runs at 8.3% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 3.9\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 76% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7559927117199675},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 95% leaves thin coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"amber","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 55% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","11 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Growing faster than most Real Estate peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Investment Analysts\u2019 Price Target Changes for November 11th (AHR, AMBQ, ANF, ARMK, AZTA, BRX, CF, COLD, CTRE, DOC)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/investment-analysts-price-target-changes-for-november-11th-ahr-ambq-anf-armk-azta-brx-cf-cold-ctre-doc.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794433493.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.557,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"CareTrust REIT (NYSE:CTRE) Price Target Raised to $46.00","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/caretrust-reit-nysectre-price-target-raised-to-46-00.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794433492.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"How Caretrust Reit Inc. (CTRE) Affects Rotational Strategy Timing","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/39/How_Caretrust_Reit_Inc._CTRE_Affects_Rotational_Strategy_Timing_111026031002_1794341402.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794341402.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"CareTrust REIT (NYSE:CTRE) Q3 2026: FFO Up, Guidance Raised","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/midcap/caretrust-reit-nysectre-q3-2026-ffo-up-guidance-raised","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794322200.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Cohen & Steers Report